    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "In the late 1990s, minimalism reigned supreme. It was against this backdrop that the FENDI Baguette was born in 1997, inspired by a compact, understated silhouette—light enough to tuck under your arm and carry your daily essentials. The Baguette boldly defied the minimalist orthodoxy of the time, breaking the monotony of single-tone dressing with vivid color clashes, rich artisanal techniques, and daring material experimentation. It became a statement of FENDI's unapologetic spirit and quickly evolved into a cultural icon and must-have item, prized for its ability to reflect the wearer's individuality.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "text": null,
      "url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/w2mm6yo/889d080f880359c2.jpg",
      "full_url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/w2mm6yo/889d080f880359c2.jpg",
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "caption",
      "text": "Madonna carrying the Baguette at the 2000 BAFTA Awards dinner",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The Baguette® 26424 stays true to the original design—an elongated silhouette with a flap closure and a sleek magnetic FF clasp that opens with one hand. It comes with an adjustable short shoulder strap.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "text": null,
